course: dictionary
lesson: 14171
title: Changing a little: modify
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To modify something means to change it a little, usually to make it better or to suit a job. «We modified our paper boat so it would float for longer.» We did not make a new boat. We changed the one we had.
explain: Modify is a verb, so it changes its ending: modifies, modified, modifying. The noun is modification. «The teacher asked for one modification to our plan.» A modification is the small change that was made.
explain: In grammar, a word modifies another word when it describes it or changes its meaning. In «a bright red kite», the words bright and red modify kite, because they tell us more about it. To find the word being modified, ask: what is being described?
explain: Scientists can also modify living things. «Genetically modified (GM) plants have had their genes changed by scientists.» Genetically means the change is made to genes, the tiny instructions inside living things.
fact: Modify means to change something a little.
fact: Modify is a verb: I modify, he modifies, we have modified, we are modifying.
fact: The noun is modification: a modification is a small change.
fact: In grammar, adjectives and adverbs modify other words: «a quick run» and «ran quickly» both show a word being described.
fact: «Genetically modified» means the genes of a plant or animal have been changed by scientists.
exercise: «We had to modify our plan when it started to rain.» What does modify mean here? | Throw it away and never think about it again | *Change it a little to make it work | Write it down in neat capitals | Copy it exactly
exercise: In «a bright red kite», which words modify kite? | a and bright | *bright and red | a and red | red and kite
exercise: Which word is the noun from modify? | modifies | modifying | *modification | modified
test: «The designers modified the wheelchair ramp after the first test.» What did they do to the ramp? | Built a new school next to it | Took it away completely | *Changed it a little to make it better | Painted it blue
test: In «She quickly finished her sums», which word modifies finished? | her | *quickly | sums | She
exam: Which sentence uses modify correctly? | The yellow modify was loud and wobbly. | *We modified the recipe by using less sugar. | We modify ourselves into the sky every Tuesday. | Modify the lunch into a house for the dog.
